---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How AI Founder Files handles personal data under UK GDPR."
  label="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  noindex
>
  <p class="placeholder-note"><strong>[DRAFT — review before launch]</strong> This is a placeholder written for UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Replace every [bracketed item] and have it checked before the site goes live.</p>

  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> [date]</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} (“we”, “us”) is operated by [legal name of the business, company number if applicable], of [registered address]. We are the data controller for personal data collected through this website. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter subscribers:</strong> your email address, and the date and time you subscribed.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails you send us:</strong> your email address and whatever you tell us.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> our hosting provider ([Cloudflare / Netlify]) processes technical data such as IP address and browser type to deliver the site and keep it secure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This site doesn’t currently use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. [Update this section if that changes.]</p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send you the weekly newsletter: <strong>your consent</strong> (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time.</li>
    <li>To reply to your emails and handle correction requests: <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and running: <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We use [newsletter provider, e.g. Buttondown / Beehiiv] to store subscriber emails and send the newsletter, and [hosting provider] to host the site. They process data on our behalf under their own terms. We don’t sell your data. [Describe any international transfers and the safeguards used.]
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your subscription details until you unsubscribe, then delete or anonymise them within [period]. [Add retention periods for emails and any other records.]
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access your data, have it corrected or deleted, restrict or object to its use, withdraw consent, and ask for a copy in a portable format. To use these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>) if you are unhappy with how we handle your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We’ll update this page when our practices change and revise the date at the top.</p>
</PageLayout>
